---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<LegalPage title="Privacy Policy" description={`How ${site.name} handles data: no accounts, no cookies, privacy-friendly analytics.`} updated="October 3, 2026">
  <p>
    {site.name} is a catalog of Framer templates. You can browse it without an account, and it has no forms, no
    newsletter and no checkout. This page explains the little data that is involved.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    We use <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a> to count visits. It does not use cookies or local storage and does not track you across websites. It records
    aggregated data such as page views, the referring site, country, browser and device type, and page load speed.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on Cloudflare. Like any web server, Cloudflare processes your IP address and request details to
    deliver pages and protect the site from abuse. See the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>If you email us, we receive your email address and message and use them only to reply.</p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>This site does not set any cookies.</p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Template pages link to Framer, where templates are previewed, bought and remixed, and the footer links to our social
    profiles. Those sites have their own privacy policies, and they may set cookies once you visit them. Some links to
    Framer are referral links; see the <a href="/terms/">Terms</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell or share personal data and keep no visitor profiles. To ask about, correct or delete anything you have
    sent us, write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted here with a new date.</p>
</LegalPage>
